3. CHECKS (one line per check, all pass)

check 01: section order tutorRole < calculator < commitments < faq holds at 12/12 screens (compareDocumentPosition, faq found by its accordion buttons).
check 02: no horizontal scroll at 390, 768, 980 and 1280 px in en, th and zh, in every state read (document scrollWidth against clientWidth).
check 03: no clipped figure and no card text overflow: the overflow-hidden clip scan and the viewport-bleed scan report 0 offenders on every state read at every screen.
check 04: default state at 12/12 screens shows 0 money, the explain.zero line, 0 pressed presets and 0 legs (spec D-6).
check 05: presets 1 to 3 at 12/12 screens show exactly one aria-pressed button, price 3000 (D-5), the setup line, and the pinned figures 5,520/5,354.40, 12,655.69/8,010/139.37/4,506.32, 18,709.44/12,015/200.83/6,493.61.
check 06: leg count 0 to 4 at 12/12 screens gives graph leg rows equal to the count, a new leg starts at 3 students, and the identity holds.
check 07: hand edit (preset 2 then own students 5) at 12/12 screens gives 18,709.44 - 8,010 - 320.98 = 10,378.46 and clears aria-pressed (D-7).
check 08: typed extreme price 1e307 in the default state at 12/12 screens shows zero money in every money row, rate 0%, no error string, no page error, and the input accepts the value.
check 09: result rows read in spec order in en, th and zh; hero equals gross - downline - tax on all 120 state records; ownGV equals price x own students; networkGV equals price x (own + leg students); rate agrees with gross/network within 0.05pp; downline equals the sum of leg payouts; tax equals 3% of the pre-tax payout.
check 10: graph bars agree with the numbers: each bar share is within 1% of payout/gross, the shares sum to about 100%, graph gross equals result gross, track widths are equal, and leg rows equal the leg count.
check 11: the rate curve marks the current volume: the marker cx equals min(network volume, 500,000)/500,000 x 100 within 0.05 at every state, and the svg carries aria-hidden="true".
check 12: keyboard only: Tab reaches the 3 presets and all 5 inputs at 12/12 screens; every calculator focus stop has the ring (box-shadow and :focus-visible); ArrowUp changes the leg count 0 to 1 and 2 to 3; the new leg row appears with 3 students; focus stays on the input with the ring visible.
check 13: locale rendering: Thai script is present on all th screens; zh calculator text equals en text at all 4 widths (D-10); row labels are Thai on th and English on zh.
check 14: target sizes and hero: preset buttons measure 44px and inputs 44px minimum at 12/12 screens; the hero figure is 36px at 390 px and 48px above.
check 15: the result card carries aria-live="polite" and reports 7 subtree mutations after a figure change at every screen.
check 16: no layout shift when a figure changes width: price 3,000 to 30,000 with a constant explain line moves card, notes, disclaimer and section by 0 px at 12/12 screens (ux-p1-layout-refocus.json, figures 12,000 to 120,000 and hero 5,354.40 to 76,614.04).
check 17: accessibility names: at default and at preset 2, all inputs and all buttons carry accessible names, exactly one button reports pressed after a preset click and none at default, at 12/12 screens (ux-p1-a11y.json, offline recount of the stored nodes).
check 18: no page error and no NaN/Infinity/undefined/Error string in the calculator on any state at any screen.
check 19: agreement with p1-checks.json: 60 shared state records and 6 shared tab-path records compared, 0 disagreements.

