6. HARNESS SELF-CORRECTIONS (transparency)

The first main run printed 132 failures. All of them were bugs in my own
check formulas: the downline check used gross - downline instead of the
downline row; the rate check used the displayed 1-decimal rate instead of
the implied rate; the keyboard bar count forgot the "Your payout" row; the
layout disclaimer selector was scoped to the section. The corrected offline
recount over the stored records reports 0 real issues (120 state records).
The accessibility run summary counted the string "true" against boolean
true and printed a false pressedButtons failure; the offline recount of the
stored nodes reports 0 issues (12 screens). The focus screenshot first read
as a preset state; pixel sample settles it: all three preset centers are
white, the price input shows the ring rgb(6,95,70) and the focused selection.

7. OPEN OBSERVATION (nonblocking, owner decides)

F1: price typed 1e307 with 4 own students shows 4e+307 in the two volume
rows while gross, downline, tax and net show 0. No error text and no page
error appear. The required gate passes in the default state: price 1e307
shows zero money in every money row. The huge volume matches the pinned
module contract A6, which keeps networkVolume finite and gross at 0. This
is recorded as nonblocking_findings[0] in the result JSON.

8. HYGIENE

No product file, test, plan or spec changed. git status stays clean. All
writes stay in the capture directory and the two result files. The server
is stopped and the heavy lock is free. No deploy and no push.

